{"output":"I'll start by discovering the tools on the three MCP servers (tickets, inventory, docs), then read the policy documents.\n\nTicket tools aren't loaded yet; I'll search for them and begin reading docs.\n\nNow the 27 ticket bodies.\n\nNow inventory (including discontinued) and all adjustments.\n\nDecisions are drafted (discontinued: HG-3105, HG-3110). Next I need each approved request's dock history by reference.\n\nNow per-warehouse stock to choose restock destinations.\n\nPlan computed. Executing in ticket id order, starting with 1402–1409.\n\nAll 27 are processed. I'll confirm no open refund tickets remain, then write the status file.\n\nI settled all 27 open `refund` tickets in id order, and a final search shows none left open. I wrote `/app/STATUS.json` with status `success`.\n\n- **Refunded (20, resolved):** 1402, 1403, 1404, 1406, 1409, 1413, 1414, 1416, 1417, 1421, 1422, 1424, 1426, 1428, 1429, 1431, 1432, 1433, 1434, 1436.\n  - Opened units had the 15% restocking fee, or 25% for electronics.\n  - Ticket 1402's unit had already been cleared to `north`, so I moved no stock for it.\n  - Unopened and opened units were restocked in the warehouse holding the fewest units of that item at the time.\n  - 1417 (hammock) and 1424 (food processor) were defective, so I wrote them off with a `damage` adjustment instead of restocking.\n- **Not refundable (5, closed):**\n  - Return window expired: 1412, 1420, 1427, 1437. Ticket 1434 (delivered 2026-08-02) stayed in time only because the summer notice adds 21 days.\n  - Final sale: 1418. The projector, HG-3105, is discontinued and not defective.\n- **Awaiting return (2, pending):** 1415 had 2 of 3 units received and 1435 had 0 of 1. I moved no stock for either.\n\nEvery stock movement used the reference `RTN-<ticket id>`. I did not re-read the inventory after the final moves. Each adjustment call returned the expected new quantity for its warehouse.","final_output":"I settled all 27 open refund tickets in id order,